  m_text: "<voffset=0.4em><b><size=0em>\u3000</size></b></voffset>\r\n<voffset=0.3em><b><size=1.4em>Get
    started</size></b></voffset>\r\n- Click <space=0.2em><mark=#FFFFFF3C padding=\"25,25,0,0\">[New
    Song]</mark><space=0.2em>. This creates a new song for you and a beginner drive
    chart to go along with it.\r\n- Go to <space=0.2em><mark=#FFFFFF3C padding=\"25,25,0,0\">[Song
    data]</mark><space=0.2em>\r\n  - Most important: <space=0.2em><mark=#FFFFFF3C
    padding=\"25,25,0,0\">[Select Audio]</mark><space=0.2em> and set the BPM of the
    song\r\n  - You may need to do some additional tweaking to get the beats matched
    up with your song: for this you can use the <space=0.2em><mark=#FFFFFF3C padding=\"25,25,0,0\">[Beat
    Offset]</mark><space=0.2em> field, and the <space=0.2em><mark=#FFFFFF3C padding=\"25,25,0,0\">[Listen]</mark><space=0.2em>
    button in the bottom right can help you with quickly tweaking this until it's
    just right\r\n  - (And you can set more metadata of the song and chart in the
    Song Data and Chart Data menus)\r\n- Place your first word with <space=0.2em><mark=#FFFFFF3C
    padding=\"25,25,0,0\">Tab</mark><space=0.2em>\r\n- See with <space=0.2em><mark=#FFFFFF3C
    padding=\"25,25,0,0\">Spacebar</mark><space=0.2em> how it plays! And press <space=0.2em><mark=#FFFFFF3C
    padding=\"25,25,0,0\">Escape</mark><space=0.2em> to go back\r\n\r\n<voffset=0.3em><b><size=1.4em>Misc
    info</size></b></voffset>\r\n- The fancy visualisation of the audio file in the
    editor isn't active for MP3 files. Well, OGG files are better anyway <space=0.2em><mark=#FFFFFF3C
    padding=\"25,25,0,0\">\xAF\\_(\u30C4)_/\xAF</mark><space=0.2em>\r\n- Behind the
    scenes, a <space=0.2em><mark=#FFFFFF3C padding=\"25,25,0,0\">song</mark><space=0.2em>
    has a folder with a <space=0.2em><mark=#FFFFFF3C padding=\"25,25,0,0\">song.json</mark><space=0.2em>
    for shared data, and one or multiple <space=0.2em><mark=#FFFFFF3C padding=\"25,25,0,0\">.drive</mark><space=0.2em>
    files, which are the difficulties. When loading a drive chart, you have to pick
    one of these <space=0.2em><mark=#FFFFFF3C padding=\"25,25,0,0\">.drive</mark><space=0.2em>
    files.\r\n- The <space=0.2em><mark=#FFFFFF3C padding=\"25,25,0,0\">[Reload]</mark><space=0.2em>
    button relentlessly reloads the currently opened drive chart, discarding all
    changes made since the last time you <space=0.2em><mark=#FFFFFF3C padding=\"25,25,0,0\">[Save]</mark><space=0.2em>d.
    Tread with care!\r\n<voffset=0.4em><b><size=0em>\u3000</size></b></voffset>\r\n"
